## Global Search

```http
GET /search?q=Tulus
```

Searches simultaneously across tracks, artists, and albums using fuzzy string matching and multi-factor relevance scoring.

---

## Search Architecture & Algorithm

Lament API utilizes a high-speed, multi-stage search engine combining in-memory Levenshtein fuzzy matching, SQLite FTS5 Full-Text Search for lyrics, and single-shot batch querying:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Client["Client Keystroke ('q')"] --> FrontendOpt["Frontend: AbortController & Local Map Cache"]
    FrontendOpt --> CacheCheck{"Backend Cache (60s)?"}
    CacheCheck -- Hit --> CachedResp["Instant Response (1-2ms)"]
    CacheCheck -- Miss --> FuzzyRAM["1. In-Memory Fuzzy Match on Artists (RAM sub-1ms)"]
    FuzzyRAM --> FTS["2. Tokenize & Sanitize FTS5 Lyrics Query (q >= 3 chars)"]
    FTS --> BatchSQL["3. Single-Shot HTTP Batch to Turso: db.batch([Tracks, Albums, Artists])"]
    BatchSQL --> Ranking["4. Rank: Title Match (100) > Lyrics / Artist Match (50) > play_count DESC"]
    Ranking --> Result["5. Return JSON & Populate 60s Cache"]
```

---

## High-Performance FTS5 Lyrics Search

Unlike traditional relational queries that perform expensive $O(N)$ sequential scans (`LIKE %q%`), Lament indexes all song lyrics inside an inverted index using SQLite **FTS5**:

- **FTS5 Inverted Index**: Lyrics are pre-tokenized into word dictionaries. When a user forgets the track title and searches a snippet of lyrics (e.g. `"terlanjur mencinta"`), the query matches via `lyrics_fts MATCH ?` in **~15ms – 100ms** (down from 2.3s+).
- **Automated Triggers**: Any lyrics scraped or updated are instantly synced to `lyrics_fts` via database triggers (`lyrics_ai`, `lyrics_au`, `lyrics_ad`).
- **Single-Shot Batch Roundtrip**: Tracks, albums, and artists are requested together using `db.batch([...], 'read')`, reducing 4 sequential HTTP network hops to just **1 single connection**.

---

## Scoring Calculation Matrix

Each track match receives a calculated ranking based on match location and popularity:

| Match Type | Weight | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Track Title Match** | `100` | Title starts with or contains query (`tracks.title LIKE %q%`) |
| **Artist Direct / Fuzzy Match** | `50` | Direct match or typo-tolerant Levenshtein lookup (sub-1ms in RAM) |
| **FTS5 Lyric Content Match** | `50` | Inverted index match inside song lyrics (`lyrics_fts MATCH ?`) |

---

## Tiebreaker & Sorting Rules

Results are ordered using an optimized 3-tier tiebreaker:

```sql
ORDER BY (CASE WHEN t.title LIKE ? THEN 100 ELSE 50 END) DESC, t.play_count DESC, t.created_at DESC
```

1. **Title Priority**: Exact or substring title matches appear first.
2. **Popularity (`play_count`)**: Tracks matching lyrics or artists are sorted by total plays.
3. **Recency (`created_at`)**: Ties are sorted by newest added tracks.

---

## Request Spec

### Headers

- `x-api-key`: `<your_client_api_key>` (or `Authorization: Bearer <key>`)

### Query Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `q` | string | Required | Search query string |
| `limit` | integer | `10` | Max results per section |

---

